  "story": "Final mission: the swarm charts the station's flight paths, and the station comes fully online.\n\nRemember the drone homing steps from Mission 5? From x, a drone halves x when it's even and goes to `3x + 1` when it's odd, until it reaches 1. Count the steps.\n\nInput: `D n` (D = 1–16 drone threads, n = 1–3000 numbers), then n whole numbers from 1 to 1000000.\n\nOutput:\n- `most steps: X (S steps)`: the number with the most steps. If several tie, the one that comes **first** in the list.\n- `total steps: T`: all the steps added up.\n\nUse exactly D threads. D may be bigger than n.",
  "starter": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <pthread.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int drones, n;\n    scanf(\"%d %d\", &drones, &n);\n    int *values = malloc(n * sizeof(int));\n    if (values == NULL) return 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) scanf(\"%d\", &values[i]);\n\n    // D threads, each charting a slice, then combine\n\n    free(values);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
  "compileFlags": "-pthread",
