  "hints": [
    "Keep a `steps` array with one slot per number. Each thread fills the slots of its own slice, so no two threads ever write the same place and no lock is needed.",
    "On the way to 1, some paths climb past 2147483647 (from 1000000 or below!). Do the walk in a `long long`, or the step counts come out wrong (or never finish).",
    "Allocate the threads with malloc (D is only known at run time), and split with `base = n / D`, `extra = n % D` so empty slices are fine. After joining, scan `steps` in order with `>`, so the first of a tie wins."
  ],
  "solution": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <pthread.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    const int *values;\n    int *steps;\n    int from, to;\n} Slice;\n\nstatic int homing_steps(long long x) {\n    int steps = 0;\n    while (x != 1) {\n        x = x % 2 == 0 ? x / 2 : 3 * x + 1;\n        steps++;\n    }\n    return steps;\n}\n\nvoid *chart(void *arg) {\n    Slice *s = arg;\n    for (int i = s->from; i < s->to; i++) s->steps[i] = homing_steps(s->values[i]);\n    return NULL;\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    int drones, n;\n    scanf(\"%d %d\", &drones, &n);\n    int *values = malloc(n * sizeof(int));\n    int *steps = malloc(n * sizeof(int));\n    pthread_t *threads = malloc(drones * sizeof(pthread_t));\n    Slice *slices = malloc(drones * sizeof(Slice));\n    if (values == NULL || steps == NULL || threads == NULL || slices == NULL) return 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) scanf(\"%d\", &values[i]);\n\n    int base = n / drones, extra = n % drones, next = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < drones; i++) {\n        int size = base + (i < extra ? 1 : 0);\n        slices[i] = (Slice){ values, steps, next, next + size };\n        next += size;\n        pthread_create(&threads[i], NULL, chart, &slices[i]);\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < drones; i++) pthread_join(threads[i], NULL);\n\n    int best = 0;\n    long long total = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        total += steps[i];\n        if (steps[i] > steps[best]) best = i;\n    }\n    printf(\"most steps: %d (%d steps)\\n\", values[best], steps[best]);\n    printf(\"total steps: %lld\\n\", total);\n    free(values);\n    free(steps);\n    free(threads);\n    free(slices);\n    return 0;\n}\n"
}
